      "f2p_classes_intentionally_omitted": {
        "StructuredOptionsSplitterTest": "Excluded per Codex round-1 review: the test directly exercises the package-private `@Internal` helper `StructuredOptionsSplitter.splitEscaped(...)`, which would over-constrain valid solutions by requiring agents to land on the exact same helper class name. Public-API behavior is still exercised through `ConfigurationConversionsTest` and `ConfigurationParsingInvalidFormatsTest` (both go through `Configuration` / `ConfigOptions` rather than the helper directly)."
      },
      "test_compile_failure_pre_state": "Expected: at base, ConfigOption / Configuration / ReadableConfig lack the new methods or types exercised by the F2P tests; eval_tests.patch references them, so flink-core's test-compile fails in pre-state. Because test-compile is module-scoped, ALL tests in flink-core (including ConfigurationTest and UnmodifiableConfigurationTest, which on their own would compile) surface as ERROR (no Surefire reports). The F2P set therefore mirrors the PR's full modified-test-file inventory minus the helper-leaking StructuredOptionsSplitterTest.",
      "p2p_isolation": "flink-clients is unchanged by either patch; its tests load the existing Configuration API which the PR preserves, so all 47 original P2P methods pass in both pre and post states. Together with the 3 synthesized sidecar P2P selectors, the union P2P suite has 50 entries.",
      "p2p_method_level_rationale": "47 original method-level P2P selectors drawn from 14 distinct flink-clients test classes. Method-level selection keeps the P2P suite focused on pre-existing downstream Configuration compatibility behavior while avoiding unrelated, JVM-specific quirks at this Flink 1.10 base."
    },
    "module_scope_rationale": "The PR only touches flink-core (production + test side). flink-clients is the smallest downstream consumer of flink-core with stable, fast tests, and serves as the P2P canary. flink-runtime + flink-streaming-java would also work but pull in significantly larger build trees at this commit."
  },
